#+TITLE: alfe-windows-old-exe-left-suspended -- a suspended alfe.exe-old* process was left running on the Windows runner
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

pjb, 2026-10-23, on PF5S26B after the AutoCAD-left-open episode
(alfe-cad-quit-saves-modified-drawing): a SUSPENDED process named
alfe.exe-old* was still running; pjb terminated it.

* What is known / supposed

- On Windows a running .exe cannot be overwritten, so a rebuild of
  alfe-sbcl.exe while an alfe still runs renames the old image aside --
  hence the "-old" name (find which build step does the rename:
  autolisp-front-end/Makefile / tools/alfe build, or the job scripts).
- Its parent was most likely the alfe of the earlier dxf-angles AutoCAD run
  whose AutoCAD sat on the Save changes prompt: alfe waits for the engine,
  the job timed out or ended, and nothing killed the alfe process (a CI job
  kill on Windows does not always reach grandchildren).
- "Suspended": not known why -- it may be the state Windows shows for a
  process whose console window was closed, or a debugger / a job object.

* To do

1. Find the rename (grep the build for "-old").
2. Make the runner's pre-job sweep (scripts/sweep-orphaned-cad.ps1) also
   end leftover alfe*.exe / alfe*.exe-old* processes from earlier jobs
   (by image path under the runner's build directory), and report them.
3. Check that a CI job that times out kills alfe and its CAD (job objects /
   taskkill /T).
